	(text "inverting config\n-> for Rthevenin << Rfeedback : hysteresis-width ~ independant from treshold center\n-> source impedance does not influence thresholds\n\nwith 1.5V swing from photointerruptor we expect 3.3V (high) -> 1.8V (low)\n-> set center threshold to ~ 2.55V  \n-> currently: switching threshold: 2.42V, hysteresis: 240mV"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 469.392 41.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "337a7d7f-21af-4af3-b852-14137fc1133a")
	)
	(text "PD configured in Software to request fixed 12V profile"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.078 93.218 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.2381)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "356d4944-5a80-41aa-a2f6-b02072a9ee04")
	)
	(text "TLV9152 is pin compatible with MCP6002 and TLV9062D\nsupply with 5V or VBUS instead of 3V3 to avoid crossover distortion\n(and netter CMR). 5V instead of VBUS as default for compat. with TLV9062"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140.208 232.664 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "39c33760-798d-4879-a900-1268029b7e94")
	)
	(text "No CTR given in Datasheet\n\n1.)\nAt IF = 20mA -> Datasheet guaratees > 0.5mA photocurrent -> estimated worst case CTR ~0.5/20 = 2.5%\n-> worst case IC @ 10mA LED drive = 240µA\n-> For Rload = 1k -> Vlow,out = 3.3-240µA*1k = 3.1V -> only 0.2V swing\n\n2.)\nTo guarantee saturation in worst case, Rload must limit Ic to 240µA\nRload > (3.3-VCE,sat)/240µA = 13kOhm \n\n3.)\nEstimate Rload for large enough output swing:\nFor a swing of 2V -> Rload = 2/240µA = 8,3kOhm\n-> we want be rather fast, so try with a smaller Rload first\n\nhttps://josepheoff.github.io/posts/rpm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 324.866 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3e602468-1fea-4afa-81f0-88a957a4d3ea")
	)
