	)
	(text "VM:  4.5-V to 33-V supply rail\nf_{PWM}: 0 - 200kHz\nlogic inputs: 100k internal PD\nIN1 = IN2 = 0 for t>1.5ms : low power mode\n\nIN1 = 1 && IN2 = 0 -> Forward\nIN1 = 1 && IN2 = 1 -> Slow decay\nIN1 = 0 && IN2 = 0 -> Fast decay\n\nForward with coast (coast = async. fast decay) :\nIN1: 1 -> 0, IN2: always 0\n\nForward with break (break = slow decay) :\nIN2: 0 -> 1, IN1: always 1\n\nFor \"manual\" Back-EMF measurement with uC, I will test Forward with coast. Let´s see if\n1.) speed stays ~const. for low duty cycles (until which D_{min} = ?}\n2.) current decays fast enough at high duty cycles/PWM freq. to still\nbeing able to measure back-EMF (decay with t ~ L / (2*(rDS_{on}+R_{Motor})) )\nOtherwise we would need to shortly inverse -> complex!\n\nIf back-EMF measurement is NOT used, use Forward with break\nfor smoother torque, less speed variation at low duty cycles"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 463.55 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dd95bfb9-3144-4cd1-9b25-ec372cac131c")
	)
